    "unit_reason":"A complete six-entry lookup record assesses consistent row/column reading across both IV row-step regimes; six isolated clicks would merely duplicate the same operation.",
    "losses":["Recognition of a supplied complete list does not establish independent transcription of six roots.","The reduced literal-cell table removes searching a full historical table page; direct-main extraction has limited mathematical demand and is not evidence of calculation fluency."],
    "options":[
      {"id":"A","text":"$(2.074,\\ 2.490,\\ 2.983,\\ 3.162,\\ 7.071,\\ 8.660)$","truth":"correct","derivation":"Read main column0 on rows4.3,6.2,8.9,10,50,75 in exactly the radicand order.","misconception":null},
      {"id":"B","text":"$(2.074,\\ 2.983,\\ 2.490,\\ 3.162,\\ 7.071,\\ 8.660)$","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Read the6.2 and8.9 rows correctly but reverse their entries when transcribing the ordered answer list.","misconception":"Transposition of adjacent input-output correspondences."},
      {"id":"C","text":"$(2.074,\\ 2.490,\\ 2.983,\\ 3.162,\\ 8.660,\\ 7.071)$","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Use the75 row for50 and the50 row for75 while preserving the first four entries.","misconception":"Transposition of the two high-radicand row lookups."}
    ]
  },
  {
