  {
    "id":"q04","source_number":"806","task_ids":["d1","d2","d3"],
    "mode":"single","concepts":[0,1,16],
    "stem":"For this calculation, first round each radicand to four significant figures, then use lower-main addition in the supplied table. Which record gives the rounded arguments and roots for $1.0058,6.83251,20.156$?",
    "table_ids":["r1.006","r6.833","r20.16"],
    "unit_reason":"A paired argument/result record tests preprocessing together with correction arithmetic instead of replacing the original higher-resolution inputs.",
    "losses":["This explicitly selected four-significant-figure preprocessing does not assess an extended-correction solution to the original unrounded arguments.","Selecting the paired record does not demonstrate independent rounding and written lookup production."],
    "options":[
      {"id":"A","text":"Arguments: $(1.006,6.833,20.16)$; roots: $(1.003,2.614,4.490)$.","truth":"correct","derivation":"Round at the fifth significant digit; then1.000+.003,2.613+.001,4.483+.007.","misconception":null},
      {"id":"B","text":"Arguments: $(1.006,6.833,20.16)$; roots: $(1.000,2.613,4.483)$.","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Preprocess correctly but stop at each lower main root before adding the correction.","misconception":"Rounding an input is incorrectly treated as eliminating its fourth-digit correction."},
      {"id":"C","text":"Arguments: $(1.006,6.833,20.16)$; roots: $(1.006,2.615,4.497)$.","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Double each correct correction:1.000+2*.003,2.613+2*.001,4.483+2*.007.","misconception":"Apply the fourth-digit correction twice, once for the original and again for the rounded radicand."}
    ]
  },
