  {
    "id":"q15","source_number":"812","task_ids":["method-comparison"],
    "mode":"multiple","concepts":[0,16],
    "stem":"Compare evaluating $\\sqrt2\\,\\sqrt3$ by obtaining the roots separately and multiplying, with simplifying the exact product before lookup. In the separate-root calculation, $\\sqrt3=\\sqrt{75}/5$ may be used with the supplied cells. Select every true statement.",
    "table_ids":["r2","r75","r6"],
    "unit_reason":"Native multiple selection separates the numerical outcome, exact identity and convenience judgment, without combination codes or a forced one-true pattern.",
    "losses":["Recognition of valid comparison statements does not establish a learner-authored explanation or production of the computations.","The bounded excerpt obtains sqrt3 through sqrt75/5 rather than navigating to an uncaptured sqrt3 main cell; original direct separate-root lookup navigation is not assessed."],
    "options":[
      {"id":"A","text":"The separate-root table calculation gives $1.414(8.660/5)=2.449048$.","truth":"correct","derivation":"Captured8.660/5=1.732;1.414*1.732=2.449048.","misconception":null},
      {"id":"B","text":"The exact product is $\\sqrt5$, so one lookup at $5$ replaces the two roots.","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Incorrectly move a product under one radical as addition: sqrt2*sqrt3 ->sqrt(2+3).","misconception":"Adding radicands when multiplying roots."},
      {"id":"C","text":"Simplifying to $\\sqrt6$ gives the table number $2.449$ and avoids multiplying two separately rounded roots.","truth":"correct","derivation":"The nonnegative-root product theorem givessqrt6 exactly; its literal main value2.449 requires only the single root lookup.","misconception":null},
      {"id":"D","text":"The separate-root table product is exactly $2.449$.","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Round2.449048 tofour significant figures and then identify that rounded display with the unrounded table-factor product.","misconception":"Conflating the exact arithmetic product of table numbers with its final rounded display."}
    ]
  },
  {
