    "losses":["Recognizing a complete sign partition is not evidence of constructing it or drawing the graph independently.","Pixels do not specify exact numerical crossing coordinates; named actual crossings preserve exact sets while approximate readings remain explicitly approximate."],
    "options":[
      {"id":"A","text":"Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx0.6,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$; negative $[-6,\\alpha)\\cup(\\beta,\\gamma)$; positive $(\\alpha,\\beta)\\cup(\\gamma,8]$.","truth":"correct","derivation":"Read thethree crossings; movingright the curve signs are-,+,-,+; include nonzero finite endpoints-6,8 and exclude all zerosfrom strict sets.","misconception":null},
      {"id":"B","text":"Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx0.6,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$; negative $(\\alpha,\\beta)\\cup(\\gamma,8]$; positive $[-6,\\alpha)\\cup(\\beta,\\gamma)$.","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Locate crossings correctly but call below-axis segmentspositive and above-axis segmentsnegative.","misconception":"Reversing the sign of graph ordinates."},
      {"id":"C","text":"Readings $\\alpha\\approx-4,\\beta\\approx0.6,\\gamma\\approx3$; zeros $\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$; negative $[-6,\\alpha]\\cup[\\beta,\\gamma]$; positive $[\\alpha,\\beta]\\cup[\\gamma,8]$.","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Use the correct sign regions but include eachzero as anendpoint in both strict-sign sets.","misconception":"Treating strict positive/negative inequalities as non-strict at the crossings."}
    ]
